  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "clear the entry\u2019s timer pointer before dropping a node whose expiration is unset, and return a descheduling event.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "2. Fallible initialization can panic an unrelated infallible caller\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `crate/src/sync/value_initializer.rs:348`, `crate/src/future/value_initializer.rs:592`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`get_with` identifies its waiters using `TypeId::of::<()>()`. This collides with `try_get_with` when its error type is `()`. A waiting `get_with` can receive the other operation\u2019s error and execute `unreachable!()`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `unit_error_collision` and `future_collision` start `try_get_with` first, then a concurrent `get_with` for the same key. Returning `Err(())` from the first initializer caused the second caller to panic in both implementations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "use a private marker type to distinguish infallible initialization from every caller-supplied error type.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
