  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `crate/src/sync/base_cache.rs:971`, `crate/src/future/base_cache.rs:1115`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Concurrent `invalidate_all` calls can store their timestamps out of order. An older timestamp overwrites a newer one, making entries valid again despite a completed invalidation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `invalidate_all_race` runs concurrent invalidators while another thread repeatedly inserts, invalidates, and reads one key. Invalidated values reappeared in all four runs, within 212 iterations.\n\n"
