  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Cancelling get_with strands other callers waiting on the same key. src/future/value_initializer.rs:189. When a future::Cache::get_with initializer is pending and a second get_with for the same missing key has started waiting on its waiter, dropping the first get_with future leaves the shared waiter in Computing. The normal completion code is the only path that removes the waiter, so the follower never executes its own initializer and remains pending indefinitely. Cancelling one cache fill can therefore permanently block further fills for that key.\n\n"
