    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "contains_key extends time-to-idle and keeps unchecked values alive. src/sync/base_cache.rs:198. With a time_to_idle policy, sync::Cache::contains_key follows the successful lookup path that records a new last-access time. Repeated membership checks at intervals shorter than the idle timeout therefore refresh an entry even if its value is never read. For example, with a ten-second idle timeout, contains_key at six and nine seconds makes the original value remain readable at ten seconds, allowing a membership poller to prevent idle expiration.\n\n"
